 & =4+10-6(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =14-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{5}{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489203 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489203 #edb/ref 1069 "q-114870" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489203 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489203 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int \\frac{6x+5}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489203 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "338fe155-640c-56d4-b9a0-1883a5de5f4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489203 #edb/ref 1074 "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ 3 & 6 & 5 \\\\  & ↓ & 18 \\\\  & 6 & 23\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{6x+5}{x-3}=6+\\frac{23}{x-3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6x+5}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6+\\frac{23}{x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\text{d}x+23\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6x+23\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489229 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489054 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489229 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489229 #edb/ref 1069 "q-352210" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489229 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489229 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{6x+5}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489229 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "660f8bdc-c1bb-5f91-9301-9db16573b0bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489229 #edb/ref 1074 "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we 