{7x-2}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(7-\\frac{13}{3x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[7{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x-13{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[7x-\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[7(1-0)-\\frac{13}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[7-\\frac{13\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}-\\frac{13}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489241 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489241 #edb/ref 1069 "q-114884" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489241 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489241 #edb/ref 1071 "${\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}-11x+15}{x-5}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489241 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "917d59cb-0d0e-5982-9eaf-dc58471e2414" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489241 #edb/ref 1074 "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 5 & 1 & -11 & 15 \\\\  & ↓ & 5 & -30 \\\\  & 1 & -6 & -15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-11x+15}{x-5}=x-6-\\frac{15}{x-5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}-11x+15}{x-5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(x-6-\\frac{15}{x-5})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x-6{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\text{d}x-15{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{x-5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{4}-6x\\,{|}_{0}^{4}-15\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-5|\\,{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({4}^{2}-{0}^{2})-6(4-0)-15(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4-5|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0-5|) \\\\  & =8-24-15(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) \\\\  & =15\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489256 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489256 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489256 #edb/ref 1069 "q-358832" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489256 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489256 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-6}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489256 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a5f0f6e3-4d12-5d35-95c5-617c3f9ade1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489256 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-6}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-6}{2(x+1/2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-6}{(x+1/2)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $5$ | $-6$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n|  | $5$ | $-\\frac{17}{2}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-6}{(x+1/2)} & =5-\\frac{(17/2)}{(x+1/2)} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{17}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-6}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(5-\\frac{17}{2x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x-17{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[5x-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5(1-0)-\\frac{17}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5-\\frac{17\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489259 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489259 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489259 #edb/ref 1069 "q-347279" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489259 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489259 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,16\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489259 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "acd22109-423d-5919-a6a9-ac45c008ca7e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489259 #edb/ref 1074 "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-15$ |\n|  | $5$ | $-16$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x-1}{x+3}=5-\\frac{16}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(5-\\frac{16}{x+3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-16{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5x\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =5(2-0)-16(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+3|) \\\\  & =10-16(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =10-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{5}{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489260 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489260 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489260 #edb/ref 1069 "q-358833" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489260 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489260 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4x-5}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{19}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489260 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ae6c8955-529c-5030-96d7-68d6213f0d1e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489260 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4x-5}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4x-5}{3(x+1/3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4x-5}{(x+1/3)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{3}$ | $4$ | $-5$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{4}{3}$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-\\frac{19}{3}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-5}{(x+1/3)} & =4-\\frac{(19/3)}{(x+1/3)} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{19}{3x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4x-5}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-\\frac{19}{3x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-19{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[4x-\\frac{19}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4(2-0)-\\frac{19}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[8-\\frac{19\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{19}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489275 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489275 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489095 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489275 #edb/ref 1069 "q-352439" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489275 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489275 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-4}{4x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{31}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489275 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "db6f337c-1879-5d7b-9da6-28f2e468ffa7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489275 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-4}{4x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-4}{4(x+\\frac{3}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{3}{4}$ | $5$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{15}{4}$ |\n|  | $5$ | $-\\frac{31}{4}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{4})} & =5-\\frac{(\\frac{31}{4})}{(x+\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{31}{4x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-4}{4x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(5-\\frac{31}{4x+3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-31{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4x+3}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[5x-\\frac{31}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+3|]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[5(2-0)-\\frac{31}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|11|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[10-\\frac{31}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{11}{3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{31}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{11}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489288 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489288 #edb/ref 1069 "q-49356" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489288 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489288 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489288 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f013a040-e69b-50f7-a6cc-a90f687ce812" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489288 #edb/ref 1074 "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\  & 2 & -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x-1}{x-1}=2{x}^{2}-x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{x}^{2}-x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{0}^{1}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1}+x{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2[\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{0}^{3}}{3}]-[\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}]+[1-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489293 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489293 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489293 #edb/ref 1069 "q-352232" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489293 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489293 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{15x+4}{x+6}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,86\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489293 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f97a62fc-8484-5bdf-88ea-0edae07612ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489293 #edb/ref 1074 "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-6$ | $15$ | $4$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-90$ |\n|  | $15$ | $-86$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{15x+4}{x+6}=15-\\frac{86}{x+6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{15x+4}{x+6}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}(15-\\frac{86}{x+6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =15{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\text{d}x-86{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{x+6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =15x\\,{|}_{1}^{5}-86\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+6|\\,{|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =15(5-1)-86(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5+6|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+6|) \\\\  & =60-86(\\operatorname{ln}⁡11-\\operatorname{ln}⁡7) \\\\  & =60-86\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{11}{7}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
